On the back of the Declaration of Independence, this phrase was written: "The original document of independence, dated July 4, 1776." The text appears reversed at the bottom of the document.
Although nobody knows who wrote it, it is well known that this large manuscript, in its early days (measuring 29¾ inches by 24½ inches), was kept hanging for storage.
Therefore, there is a possibility that the note might simply be attached as a label.
