Moreover, between each dynasty, there was an unstable period during which provinces were divided. The most famous era was the Three Kingdoms period, which lasted for 60 years between the Han and Jin dynasties.
During this period, intense wars took place among many nobles who were fighting for the throne.
These three kingdoms are considered one of the bloodiest periods in ancient Chinese history, during which thousands of people lost their lives in the struggle to seize the highest throne in the great palace of Xi'an.
