Shared taxis are one of the fast and convenient ways to travel to nearby locations such as Paro (Nu 150) and Punakha (Nu 200).
The Oiapoque River Bridge is a cable bridge. This bridge is built over the Oiapoque River to connect the cities of Oiapoque in Brazil and Saint-Georges de l'Oyapock in French Guiana.
The height of the two towers is 83 meters, their length is 378 meters, and they have two lanes each with a width of 3.50 meters.
The vertical clearance under Tower 15 is 15 meters. Its construction was completed in August 2011, and it was opened for public use in March 2017.
The completion date of the bridge is September 2017, which is the expected time for the completion of the customs stations.
The Guaraní were the most significant indigenous group inhabiting present-day eastern Paraguay, living a semi-nomadic lifestyle based on hunting and practicing subsistence agriculture.
The Chaco region was also home to other indigenous groups such as the Guaycurú and Payaguá, who sustained themselves through hunting, gathering, and fishing.
In the 16th century, Paraguay, which had previously been known as the "Vast Province of India," emerged as a result of the encounters between Spanish conquistadors and native groups.
The Spanish began their colonial period, which lasted for three centuries.
Since the establishment of Asunción in 1537, Paraguay has managed to preserve many of its indigenous characteristics and traits.
Argentina is renowned for having one of the best national teams and the best players in the world.
The biggest event of the year takes place in December at the "Las Canitas" polo fields.
Tournaments and smaller competitions can also be observed here at other times of the year.
For information about polo match news and ticket purchase locations, check Asociacion Argentina de Polo.
The official currency of the Falkland Islands is the Falkland Islands pound (FKP), which is pegged at the value of one British pound (GBP).
At the only bank in the islands, located in Stanley and adjacent to the FIC West shop, currency exchange is available.
Pounds sterling are generally accepted throughout the islands, and both Visa and American dollar cards are also commonly accepted.
Credit cards may not be accepted on more remote islands, although British pounds and US dollars are generally accepted; therefore, coordinate the accepted payment method in advance with the owners.
It is almost impossible to exchange Falkland Islands currency outside the islands, so exchange your money before leaving the islands.
Since Montevideo is located near the equator, when it is winter in the Northern Hemisphere, it is summer there, and vice versa.
Montevideo is a semi-tropical region; during the summer months, temperatures usually rise above 30 degrees Celsius.
Winter can be deceptively cold: although temperatures rarely drop below freezing, wind and humidity work together to make you feel colder than the thermometer indicates.
There is no distinct dry or rainy season: rainfall remains almost constant throughout the year.
Although many animals in the park have become accustomed to seeing humans, wild animals are still wild, and we must not feed them or disturb them.
According to park authorities, keep a minimum distance of 100 meters from bears and wolves, and 25 meters from other wild animals!
American bison, deer, moose, bears, and almost all large animals, no matter how tame they may seem, can attack.
Every year, dozens of visitors are injured due to failing to maintain a safe distance. These are large, wild, and inherently dangerous animals, so do not enter their vicinity.
Moreover, keep in mind that odors attract bears and other wild animals, so avoid carrying or cooking fragrant foods and keep your campsite clean.
Apia is the capital of the country of Samoa. This city is located on the island of Upolu and has a population of slightly less than 40,000.
Apia was founded in the 1850s and has been the official capital of Samoa since 1959.
