Due to Auckland's location between two harbors, many coastlines exist. The most popular ones are located in three areas.
The North Shore (in the North Harbour area) lies in the Pacific Ocean and stretches from Long Beach in the north to Donport in the south.
They are almost all sandy beaches where swimming is safe, and most of them have shade from pohutukawa trees.
The Tamaki Drive beaches in the Waitemata Harbour are located in the suburbs of the renowned cities of Mission Bay and Saint Heliers in central Auckland.
These are family-friendly beaches, which can sometimes be crowded and feature good shops along the shoreline. Swimming is safe.
