If you're not used to driving on rural roads, stay alert: there are more steep slopes, narrow lanes, and sharp turns.
The posted speed limits are significantly lower than those in the preceding and following sections—typically 35 to 40 mph (56 to 64 km/h)—and strict adherence to them is even more critical than in other sections.
