German pastries are excellent and diverse and rich in Bavaria, resembling mostly what is cooked in the southern neighbor, Austria.
Fruit pastries are common. Apple pastries are baked throughout the year, and in summer, cherries and plums are used for decoration.
Many German pastries contain almonds, walnuts, and other tree nuts. Popular cakes are often served with a cup of strong coffee.
If you're looking for small but filling pastries, simply try something known as Berliner, Pfannkuchen, or Krapfen, depending on your region.
Kari is a dish prepared with herbs and spices, along with meat or vegetables.
Depending on the amount of liquid present, the condition can be "dry" or "moist."
In central northern India and Pakistan, yogurt is usually used in karhi stew; in southern India and some coastal regions of the subcontinent, coconut milk is commonly used.
Indonesian cuisine is a broad term encompassing a wide diversity of regional cooking across this nation, as Indonesia offers the ability to choose from among 17,000 islands.
However, in the absence of additional qualifications, this term originally means "food" and is derived from the central and eastern parts of the main island of Java.
Javanese cuisine, which is now widely available throughout the Indonesian archipelago, features a range of simple, flavorful dishes, with dominant Javanese seasonings being peanuts, chili, sugar (especially Javanese coconut sugar), and various aromatic spices.
The stirrup is a support for the rider's foot, hanging from both sides of the saddle.
Although they provide greater stability for the rider, they may pose safety concerns because the rider's feet could get caught in them.
If a rider falls off a horse and their foot gets caught in the stirrup, the horse may drag them along the ground if it runs away. To minimize this risk, many precautionary measures can be taken.
First of all, most motorcycle racers wear motorcycle boots that have a heel and a narrow, completely slim toe.
In the next stage, some saddles—especially English saddles—have safety girths that allow the stirrup leathers to detach from the saddle in case the rider falls off the horse.
In Cochamó—the top climbing destination in Chile, known as South America's Yosemite—there are various types of walls and granite cliffs.
From the highest point, one can enjoy breathtaking views of the peaks. Climbers continuously create new routes across numerous paths and potentially sheer cliffs from all corners of the world.
Winter sports on slopes, such as skiing and snowboarding, are popular activities in which you descend down snowy, sloping terrains using ski poles or a snowboard attached to your feet.
Skiing is the main activity of the trip, which has a large number of enthusiasts and is sometimes known as "ski touring," meaning planning the entire vacation around skiing at a specific location.
Skiing is an extremely ancient activity—the origin of cave paintings depicting skiers dates back to 5000 BC.
Skiing on hills dates back to at least the 17th century, and in 1861, the Norwegians established the first recreational ski club in Australia.
Skiing trip: This activity is also called backcountry skiing, ski touring, or ski walking.
This is related to it, but usually does not include alpine skiing tours or alpine climbing; the latter is performed on steep terrain and requires skis and sturdier crampons.
Just as you consider the hiking trail, also think about the skiing trail.
Under good weather conditions, you can cover a significantly greater distance than normal walking— but it rarely happens that you can reach cross-country skiing speed without carrying a heavy backpack on well-maintained trails.
Europe is a relatively small continent, yet it has many independent countries. Under normal circumstances, traveling between numerous countries requires going through multiple visa application processes and passport controls.
Nevertheless, the Schengen area functions like a country in this regard.
As long as you stay in this area, you can generally cross borders without going through passport control again.
Similarly, with a Schengen visa, there is no need to apply for a visa separately for each of the Schengen member countries, thus saving you time, money, and paperwork.
There is no global definition for considering items as antiques. Some tax authorities consider items older than 100 years to be antiques.
This definition varies geographically, particularly in regions such as North America, where the age restriction may be lower than in Europe.
Handicraft products may be considered antiques, even though they are newer than mass-produced similar items.
Rearing Arctic goats is a vital livelihood among the Sami, and the cultural exchange surrounding its trade is also significant for many other professions.
Although not all Semites were traditionally involved in raising large goats, they sustained themselves through fishing, hunting, and similar activities, and primarily used goats as working animals.
Today, many Sami people work in modern commerce. Tourism is one of the important sources of income in Lapland, the Sami region.
