You can see the pyramids in the darkness and observe them in silence before the show begins.
You can usually always hear the sounds of tourists and vendors. The story of sound and light is just like a storybook.
Sphinx is positioned behind the scenes as the narrator of a long-standing story.
These scenes are projected onto the pyramids, and the different pyramids are illuminated.
The South Shetland Islands, discovered in 1819, are claimed by many countries and had the highest number of active bases—sixteen—in 2020.
This archipelago is located 120 kilometers north of the peninsula. Its largest island is King George, and its inhabited area is called Villa Las Estrellas (Star Village).
Other islands include Livingston and Despoten, where volcanic lakes have created a scenic natural harbor overlooking an active volcano.
Althorland is a region in the southern part of the peninsula, bounded by the Bellinghausen Sea.
The peninsula's mountains merge with the plateau here, then rise again to form a 360-kilometer-long range of the Sawtooth Mountains, which the Minnesota Glacier has split into two.
The northern part or the Sentinel Range features the highest mountain in Antarctica, Mount Vinson, which has an elevation of 4,892 meters.
