For some, understanding how airplanes work and what happens during a flight may help overcome the fear stemming from the unknown and the lack of control.
Courier companies earn good money due to the fast delivery of products. Usually, time is very important when sending business documents, goods, or spare parts for quick repairs.
In some routes, larger companies own their own aircraft, but in other routes and for smaller companies, this has been a challenge.
If they sent the goods by air mail, in some routes it could take days for the cargo to be unloaded from the airplane and cleared through customs.
The only way to get there faster was to send it as checked luggage. Aviation regulations won't allow them to send luggage without a passenger.
