However, it doesn't come cheap: a general rule states that you can expect to pay four times the usual rental rate for commercial use and eleven times that amount for first-class service!
In general, searching for discounts on business and first-class seats for flights from point A to point B yields no benefit.
Airlines well understand that a group of air travelers, under urgent circumstances, are willing to pay a high price for the benefit of fast and comfortable travel, and they set their prices accordingly.
The capital of Moldova is Chișinău. Its local language is Romanian, but Russian is widely used there.
Moldova is a multi-ethnic republic suffering from ethnic and tribal conflicts.
In 1994, this conflict led to the establishment of the self-declared republic of "Transnistria" in eastern Moldova, which has its own government and currency, but is not recognized by any member states of the United Nations.
Despite the failure of political negotiations, economic relations between these two parts of Moldova have been reestablished.
The main religion of the people of Moldova is Eastern Christianity.
Izmir is Turkey's third-largest city and the country's second-largest port after Istanbul, with a population of approximately 3.7 million, and is considered one of the most important transportation hubs in the country.
The ancient city of Smyrna, which is now a modern, developed, and bustling commercial center, was established around a vast bay surrounded by mountains.
Wide boulevards, buildings with glass facades, and modern shopping centers, among which traditional red-tiled roofs, 18th-century bazaars, and old mosques and churches stand out, make the city's atmosphere more Mediterranean European than traditionally Turkish.
The village of Hadarsvik has a view of an island near Eysturoy and features an unusual octagonal church.
In the courtyard of this church, there are some interesting marble sculptures of doves on some of the graves.
It's worth spending half an hour wandering around this charming village.
In the north, in an easily accessible area, the romantic and charming town of Sintra is located, which became famous among foreigners after being vividly and gloriously described by Lord Byron.
