Pa amb Oli is a popular simple dinner, especially during summer: bread with olive oil, tomatoes, and any available condiments such as cheese, tuna fish, and the like.
All nouns, along with the word "Sie" for you, always begin with a capital letter, even if they appear in the middle of a sentence.
This is an important method for distinguishing between certain verbs and their objects.
This also significantly eases reading, although writing is somewhat more complex and requires knowing whether a verb or adjective has been used correctly or not.
The pronunciation of Italian words is relatively simple, as the pronunciation of most words exactly matches their spelling.
The main letters you need to be careful with are c and g, as their pronunciation varies depending on the vowels that follow them.
Also, be aware that "r" and "rr" are pronounced differently: "caro" means "dear," while "carro" means "cart."
