Since light pollution was not initially considered a problem but is now regarded as one, they are usually located in cities or on university campuses, making them easier to access than those built during the modern era.
Most modern research telescopes are large facilities located in remote areas with favorable atmospheric conditions.
Viewing the cherry blossoms (hanami) has been part of Japanese culture since the 8th century.
This concept originates from China, where the flower of choice was the almond blossom.
In Japan, the first cherry blossom viewing ceremony is held by the Emperor and is exclusively for him and the close members of the imperial court.
